@page
@model DevOpsReviewA6.Pages.DemoRetailModel
@{
}

<div class="pageSize">


    <div class="bulletBox">
        <h1 class="colStructure">
            Retail Gap and Demographics
        </h1>
    </div>

    <div>
        <p>

        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="columnsContainer">

        <div class="colStructure">
            <h3>Nearest locations</h3>
            <p class="cPara">
                Currently, there are no Culver’s locations in Oklahoma,
                with the nearest restaurants located in Kansas, Arkansas, and Texas. The closet location to Stillwater is
                2 hours away in Derby Kansas, which is an absurd distance to drive for fastfood.

            </p>

            
            <img src="~/photos/nearest_culvers.png" class="picRes" alt="Stillwater to nearest Culvers" />
            <img src="~/photos/derby_culvers.png" class="picRes" alt="Culvers Derby Location" />

        </div>

       
        <div class="colStructure">
            <h3>Oklahoma Location coming 2027</h3>
            <p class="cPara">
                Oklahoma City is expected to welcome its first Culver’s in early 2027, however
                Stillwater residents would still have to travel a considerable distance to enjoy it.
                Opening a Culver’s in Stillwater would fill this retail gap.
            </p>
            <img src="~/photos/culversokc.jpg" class="picRes" alt="Culver's OKC Location" />

        </div>


        



    </div>
    <br />

    <div class="bulletBox">
        <h3>Demographics</h3>
        <p class="cPara">
            Culver's is one of the fastest growing burger chains in the United States,
            adding a net 56 stores. For comparison, Shake Shack trailed them
            with a net 50 store openings.

            However, there is not a Culver's in the state of Oklahoma.
            All states bordering Oklahoma have a combined 65 stores,
            and Stillwater should be one of the first locations in the state to get one.
        </p>

        <img src="~/photos/culvers locations.jpg"
             class="map" alt="Culver's Locations by State" />
    </div>

    
  

    <br />




</div>
